From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 15:30:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] DsRunner: take the keys of the in-game reset from
 /_pico/igr.keys

L+R+Down+B is fixed in the key check, but L and R are the first buttons
to wear out on a DS Lite: on the first hardware test they registered
only when pressed hard, so the hotkey looked broken.

The key check now loads its mask from a literal that the patcher fills
in, instead of building the constant with three instructions, so the
section keeps its size (0x40). The arm7 reads the mask from the first
line of /_pico/igr.keys ("0x08C"), before the rom is opened like
igr.off, and passes it in bits 16-25 of the IPC_COMMAND_ARM9_SET_ROM_FILE_INFO
flags word; 0 means the default L+R+Down+B (0x382). A missing file, a
value of 0 or bits above the 10 keys the arm9 can read (A, B, Select,
Start, Right, Left, Up, Down, R, L) give the default. DsRunner writes
the file from its setting "inGameResetKeys" and deletes it for the
default.

igr-log.txt names the active keys and where they came from, and the
mask that was patched in.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018ba2i77rK9QaTUSsETPJXV
